@host = http://localhost:5082
@productId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@orderId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

# Every response carries an X-Correlation-Id: that request's W3C trace id, and the value its log
# lines are written under. An inbound X-Correlation-Id is ignored, so the requests below send none —
# to join a trace you already have, send `traceparent: 00-<32 hex>-<16 hex>-01` instead.

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Provision stock for a product
# Stock does not resolve productId against Catalog: it is a leaf service.
# @name setStock
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "quantityOnHand": 10
}

### Provisioning the same product again -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "quantityOnHand": 5
}

### Read the position
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stock/{{productId}}

### Update the physical count (cannot go below what is reserved)
# The reservation lifecycle moved off HTTP in Phase 2: stock is now held only by the
# OrderPlacedConsumer, so there is no reserve/confirm/release request to send. This PUT races
# that consumer on the same row and loses with a 409 when the consumer commits first.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/stock/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityOnHand": 25
}

### Unknown product -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stock/55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555

### Negative quantity -> 400 ValidationProblemDetails
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666",
  "quantityOnHand": -5
}

### Malformed JSON -> 400 ProblemDetails (never a 500)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{
